# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 intg.cc _integrate, the 4-argument branch (G770, F470): before the exact run it integrates the integrand numerically (tegral, 1e-6, 1<<10 intervals) only to write "// ∫ ~= <value>" to the log. When the integrand holds an integral, evalf_double of it integrates the inner integral at every sample point of the outer one, and the inner call does the same again: int(int(x^2+y^2,y,0,3),x,0,2) took 1,743,911 interrupt checks (Digits 40) where int(int(x^2+y^2,y=0..3),x,0,2), which has no 4-argument call to preview, took 5,272; the triple integral of x+y+z over [0,1]x[0,2]x[0,3] 176,058,981 against 4,386. `int` and `integration` are functions of their own that call _integrate, so the guard reads their names as well as at_integrate. The preview is skipped when the integrand holds an integral call; the value, the exact run and every other integral are unchanged.
# Changed by Pascaline contributors, 2026-11-19
